## Prepared statements and parameters (don’t string-concatenate Cypher)

Kuzu supports parameterized Cypher:

* variables in the query use `$name`
* in Python you pass a dict via `parameters=...` ([Kuzu][10])

Example:

```python
conn.execute(
    """
    MATCH (p:Person)
    WHERE p.age > $min_age AND p.age < $max_age
    RETURN p.name;
    """,
    parameters={"min_age": 18, "max_age": 30},
)
```

([Kuzu][10])

This is the same “don’t build SQL strings from user input” story, just for Cypher. ([Kuzu][10])

