## Practical “don’t shoot yourself” tips

* **Design schema deliberately**: you can’t just start emitting new labels/properties forever—Kuzu wants a defined schema. ([Kuzu][1])
* **Pick good primary keys** for node tables (you must have them). ([Kuzu][1])
* **Ingest big data with `COPY FROM`**, not millions of `CREATE` statements. ([Kuzu][6])
* **Copy nodes before relationships** (bulk import rule). ([Kuzu][7])
* **Parameterize queries** (`$param` + `parameters={...}`) especially if any user input is involved. ([Kuzu][10])
* **Be aware of the embedded locking model** when mixing notebooks/CLI/tools: you can easily run into file locks if you open the same DB in multiple processes in read-write mode. ([Kuzu][5])

